---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
const updated = 'July 2026'
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy — QuoteLens" description="How QuoteLens collects, uses, and protects personal data.">

  <section class="legal">
    <p class="eyebrow">QuoteLens</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p class="todo">
      Draft for review. [LEGAL ENTITY NAME], [REGISTERED ADDRESS],
      [PRIVACY EMAIL] and [JURISDICTION] to be confirmed.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      QuoteLens is operated by [LEGAL ENTITY NAME], [REGISTERED ADDRESS].
      For any privacy question or request, contact
      <a href="mailto:[PRIVACY EMAIL]">[PRIVACY EMAIL]</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Two kinds of people use QuoteLens</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Businesses</strong> sign up for an account to offer instant
      quotes. <strong>Customers</strong> use a business's quote link to get
      a price. This policy covers both, but the roles differ: for customer
      enquiry data, the business you contacted decides how that data is
      used, and QuoteLens processes it on their behalf. For business
      account data, QuoteLens decides.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>From businesses:</strong> business name, login email, phone
    or WhatsApp number, the products and prices you configure, and account
    activity.</p>
    <p><strong>From customers:</strong> the name, phone number, location
    and (if provided) email address you enter to receive a quote; the
    measurements and product options you choose; and any photo you take or
    upload.</p>

    <h2>Photos</h2>
    <p>
      If you take or upload a photo, it is used to estimate the dimensions
      of what you are quoting and is saved with your enquiry so the
      business can see what you asked about. Photos are stored on our
      infrastructure and shared with the business you contacted. To
      estimate measurements, the photo is sent to Google's Gemini service.
      You do not have to use a photo — every quote can be completed by
      entering measurements manually.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
    <p>
      We use these providers to run the service, and they process data only
      to provide it to us:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — database, authentication and file storage</li>
      <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — hosting</li>
      <li><strong>Google (Gemini)</strong> — estimating measurements from photos</li>
      <li><strong>OpenAI</strong> — generating product reference images for businesses</li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong> — sending quote emails</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal data and we do not use it for advertising.
      When you request a quote, your enquiry details are shared with the
      business you contacted — that is the point of the service.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Enquiry data, including photos, is kept for as long as the business
      that received it keeps its account, unless they or you ask us to
      delete it. Business account data is kept while the account is active
      and for a reasonable period afterwards.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us for a copy of your data, ask us to correct it, or ask
      us to delete it. Businesses can delete their account, and everything
      in it, from the dashboard. Customers who submitted an enquiry do not
      have an account — to have your enquiry deleted, write to
      <a href="mailto:[PRIVACY EMAIL]">[PRIVACY EMAIL]</a> or contact the
      business you sent it to, as they hold their own copy.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We use a small number of cookies that are necessary to run the
      service. See our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Data is stored with access controls and encrypted in transit. No
      system is perfectly secure, but we take reasonable measures to
      protect what we hold.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>QuoteLens is intended for businesses and their customers, and is not
    directed at children.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We will update this page when our practices change, and revise the
    date at the top.</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>This policy is governed by the laws of [JURISDICTION].</p>

    <p class="back"><a href="/">← Back to QuoteLens</a></p>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>